#549 fbctrlportkill -- PRE-TABLE ADDENDUM for kill table 3, written BEFORE table 3 runs (this file's mtime is the order
proof; table3/ does not exist yet).

WHY A TABLE 3.  The §F2 pass: nine seats plus the dedicated codex (Astra) and grok jobs, then the Fable 5.1
adjudication (fable5_f2.md, on 8 of 9 seats) and the fresh Opus 5.5 measuring seat that landed after it (opus5_f2.md,
the ninth).  They changed the detector, not the fix: the device code is unchanged except the R1 comment sentence.
The Opus seat MEASURED every F2 row in its corrected form (red on its target edit, green on the fix) in a prototype;
this probe is that prototype minus its diagnostic rows, plus the adjudicated amendments and a class closure.

THE DETECTOR CHANGE (L1, pre-ship).  41 rows -> 73; 5 sessions -> 8 (C A P R K F V W).  The exit status is now 0
only when the controls are OK and every row is green (P1).  The docstring lost its `r' prefix (zero backslashes, so
the text is unchanged) so check_score_claims.py can read it at all (Fable, measured: it read 0 characters).

DIFF OF THE PRESCRIBED ROWS (PRETABLE.out and PRETABLE_ADDENDUM_t2.out) AGAINST THE NEW PROBE:
  all 41 present.  C x6 (survival, disassembly, liveness x2, X1 signature, no-(once)); A/P/K disassembly x3;
  accept x8; round-trip x7; refuse x9 + "refuse 9 after PORT=7"; announce x2; K x3; F x2.
  RENAMED, same channel: "announce: still exactly 1 after ten refusals" -> "... after twelve refusals" (sampled at the
  twelfth, tag r11).  REORDERED: P's first refusal is now 8 (was 9) -- so under M_reflatch the 9 row is the one that
  reds and the 8 row is the one refused; under M_gt the first-refusal count reds (8 accepted, no announce).
  Nothing prescribed was dropped.

NEW ROWS (32), each with the mutant(s) it is predicted to kill and the observable that differs:
